                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363 Am 6/92: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-21T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21, 1921—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 22—11 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>111. President Acosta yesterday submitted British note to Congress requesting its
                    opinion before he concludes any new agreement on the subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
